# /opt/corvid/sentinel.env: read by both the sentinel and the Stalwart container, whose plan
# references CORVID_SENTINEL_SECRET to sign the WebHook it posts here. Settings live in
# config.yaml.
# openssl rand -hex 32. Changing it invalidates every webhook Stalwart has queued.
CORVID_SENTINEL_SECRET=
# An app password used by nothing else, so it can be revoked alone. Never the account password:
# TOTP on the account (once enabled) would lock this out, and every notice the sentinel imports
# would itself count as an account-password sign-in.
CORVID_JMAP_PASSWORD=
